 ## Unreleased
 
+### Added
+- Configurable instruction-profiler module-origin range limits and retained trace
+  budgets, with module-map truncation/unavailability reported separately from
+  execution-stack detail truncation.
+- Opt-in Linux RAM-backed benchmark storage: `PocketIcBuilder::with_ram_storage`,
+  `PocketIcState::new_in_ram`, and `StartServerParams::ram_storage`, with matching
+  server `--ram` / `POCKET_IC_RAM=1` support. State and compilation caches use
+  validated executable tmpfs without changing instruction or cycle accounting.
+- Physical attempt IDs, bounded DTS slice records and exact round-work totals, including aborted paused attempts.
+  Snapshot availability and authoritative commit/discard disposition remain separate from the Wasm result;
+  runtime logical execution context links retry attempts without inventing missing causal relationships.
+- A standalone server command, `pocket-ic explain`, exports compiled computation rules, source excerpts,
+  costs, default limits and accounting explanations as self-contained JSON without creating an instance.
+- Memory trace host accounting events and totals, separate canister/subnet scopes and instruction/cycle units,
+  captured runtime limits, exact u128 prices, completeness flags and an optional runtime cursor clear guard.
+- The functions `PocketIc::start_memory_access_tracing`, `PocketIc::stop_memory_access_tracing`,
+  `PocketIc::get_memory_access_trace`, and `PocketIc::clear_memory_access_trace` to record which Wasm pages (64 KiB)
+  of the heap every message execution of a canister accessed and dirtied, and the types `MemoryAccessTrace`,
+  `TracedExecution`, and `TracedExecutionOutcome` describing the recorded executions.
+  These functions require a PocketIC server with support for memory access tracing.
+- The function `PocketIc::start_memory_access_viewer` to serve a web app showing the memory access traces of all
+  instances of the PocketIC server while they are recorded, together with a JSON API and an MCP server for agents,
+  and the types `MemoryAccessViewerConfig` and `MemoryAccessViewerInfo` of the corresponding endpoint.
+- `PocketIc::start_instruction_profiling(canister_id, max_executions)` to collect bounded instruction charge
+  profiles for selected executions through the same trace API. Memory access tracing can run without enabling
+  instruction profiling. Profiles include an installed-module hash and its hash kind; Rust source mapping requires a hash
+  of the uncompressed installed module and matching external build artifacts.
+- Explanations for recorded runtime charge rules: conditions, formulas, optimization opportunities, and excerpts
+  of the runtime implementation with source-file hashes. Per-execution rule totals reference a shared dictionary.
+
+### Changed
+- Version 2 memory access traces serialize 64-bit counters and page indices as decimal strings to preserve their
+  precision in JSON consumers. The Rust types retain `u64` fields and also accept legacy JSON numbers.
+
